in the serving runtime build pipeline and demonstrably fails a build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage (verified against a known-bad case) while passing the remediated builds.\n5. The module inventory entries for all remediated runtime images reflect the post-remediation state.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): serving data plane runtime images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules, with no non-validated crypto in the request path.\n- HLR-3 (P1, bundled): the CI FIPS regression check covering serving runtime builds is authored and verified here — it spans the same build surfaces and remediated images as the HLR-1 work, so it is not separately schedulable as its own epic.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- This surface is included because the problem statement names the serving data plane as linking non-validated crypto and HLR-1 requires all serving-stack images clean, even though the strategy's Affected Components list omits it; the discrepancy is recorded in the decomposition health warnings and should be confirmed with the strategy author.\n- If source-level changes in upstream model-server projects prove necessary (rather than midstream rebuild-level changes), the remediation approach is rewritten to include midstream patching or upstream contribution.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":63780,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-846eb023bd761b18","agent_id":"a752c525d87d20bde","session_id":"b04d48ec-e92b-4b9b-98a0-90c74f405f25","uuid":"32e503be-1bbe-4091-bbac-f79a17b35f62","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:03:22.118Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013"}
