{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-7cd5486d-9f49-4102-87b0-8ab09084c8c5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b46c0e788cd23de","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9013-_3q1wgdq/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E005.md","content":"# FIPS compliance evidence package assembly and submission\n\n## Description\n\nAssemble the FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package for the model serving stack — module inventory, build attestations, and FIPS-mode test results — and submit it through the security review board to the external accredited certification laboratory.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Collect the post-remediation module inventory produced by the serving-stack crypto audit.\n- Collect build attestations for every in-scope serving-stack image from the build pipeline identified for it (KServe components, Platform Operator, and serving data plane runtimes).\n- Collect the FIPS-mode verification results from the remediated images' cluster verification.\n- Assemble the package and validate it internally: every module-inventory entry is backed by attestations and test results; any gap is explicitly listed rather than silently missing.\n- Submit the package through the security review board process at the defined milestones to the external certification laboratory, and track it through triage.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. The evidence package contains the complete post-remediation module inventory, build attestations for every in-scope serving-stack image, and the FIPS-mode test results.\n2. The package is internally validated: every module-inventory entry has corresponding attestations and test results, and all gaps are explicitly listed.\n3. The package is submitted through the security review board to the external certification laboratory, and the submission is acknowledged and triaged.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Certification laboratory turnaround (historically six to nine months) and security review board cadence are externally controlled and cannot be compressed by engineering effort; they dominate the program schedule but gate the certification outcome, not the engineering work in this strategy.\n- The certification decision and its timing are outside engineering control; this epic's engineering completion point is submission and triage of the package.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): the compliance evidence package (module inventory, build attestations, test results) is assembled and submitted through the security review board to the external certification lab.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":64548,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-846eb023bd761b18","agent_id":"a752c525d87d20bde","session_id":"b04d48ec-e92b-4b9b-98a0-90c74f405f25","uuid":"66a64d22-3cfa-408a-9b2e-e49b9047b100","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:03:30.631Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013"}
