{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8da7b427f909cfa0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n3\ttitle: Serving-stack crypto module audit and FIPS remediation plan\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 1\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Serving-stack crypto module audit and FIPS remediation plan\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve the unknowns that gate FIPS 140-3 remediation of the model serving stack: produce a complete inventory of the cryptographic libraries linked into every serving-stack image, classify each as validated or non-validated, and determine the remediation approach and build-attestation source for each affected image. The findings feed the per-surface remediation work and form the module-inventory component of the compliance evidence package.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Enumerate all serving-stack images in scope: KServe control-plane and data-plane components, Platform Operator images, and the serving data plane model-server runtime images (vLLM, OpenVINO, Caikit-class runtimes).\n34\t- For each image, inventory the linked cryptographic libraries and modules, and classify each as validated or non-validated against the applicable cryptographic-module validation program, recording the classification source.\n35\t- For each image containing non-validated crypto, document a remediation approach (rebuild against validated modules available in the supported base images, version change, or library replacement) with rationale and risk.\n36\t- Identify, per image, the build pipeline that will produce the attestations required for the compliance evidence package; explicitly flag any gaps.\n37\t- Deliver the findings as a structured module inventory and remediation plan that the compliance evidence package can consume without rework.\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t1. Every serving-stack image in scope is enumerated, and every linked cryptographic library is classified as validated or non-validated with the classification source recorded — no unclassified linkage remains.\n42\t2. Every image classified as containing non-validated crypto has a documented remediation approach with rationale and a risk note.\n43\t3. The build-attestation source for every in-scope image is identified, or an explicit gap is recorded for follow-up.\n44\t4. The module inventory is delivered in a structured form directly consumable by the compliance evidence package.\n45\t\n46\t## HLR Traceability\n47\t\n48\t- HLR-2 (P0, partial): produces the module inventory that is a required component of the compliance evidence package.\n49\t- Enables HLR-1 (P0): determines the remediation scope and per-image approach for all serving-stack images.\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-816ef491c81f9a1e","agent_id":"a10b6399675a8b73a","session_id":"b04d48ec-e92b-4b9b-98a0-90c74f405f25","uuid":"fbf252e9-cea5-4a34-b686-098abcad03e2","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:06:02.181Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8da7b427f909cfa0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
