{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a493669515e74d19","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E002\n3\ttitle: FIPS crypto remediation of KServe component images\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the audit finds no viable validated-module remediation for\n15\t    a KServe image (a required library has no validated build), the remediation approach\n16\t    for that image is rewritten - library replacement or an upstream contribution\n17\t    - before the image can be declared FIPS-compliant.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: 1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# FIPS crypto remediation of KServe component images\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tMake every KServe component image run correctly on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters using validated cryptographic modules, with no non-validated crypto in the inference request path. This epic also authors and verifies the FIPS regression gating check that covers KServe image builds.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Apply the remediation approach determined by the serving-stack crypto audit to each KServe component image identified as linking non-validated crypto (rebuild against validated modules, version changes, or library replacement, as documented in the audit's remediation plan).\n44\t- Verify the remediated images on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster: the inference request path (InferenceService deployment through endpoint serving) exercises only validated crypto.\n45\t- Author and verify the FIPS regression gating check covering KServe image builds: the check fails any KServe build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage.\n46\t- Update the module inventory entries for the remediated KServe images to their post-remediation state, for consumption by the compliance evidence package.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t1. A post-remediation scan of every KServe component image in scope shows no non-validated cryptographic library in the request path.\n51\t2. The remediated images build green in the component build pipeline.\n52\t3. The remediated images are verified to serve inference requests correctly on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster.\n53\t4. The FIPS regression gating check is active in the KServe build pipeline and demonstrably fails a build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage (verified against a known-bad case) while passing the remediated builds.\n54\t5. The module inventory entries for all remediated KServe images reflect the post-remediation state.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- HLR-1 (P0): KServe component images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules, with no non-validated crypto in the request path.\n59\t- HLR-3 (P1, bundled): the CI FIPS regression check covering KServe builds is authored and verified here — it spans the same build surfaces and remediated images as the HLR-1 work, so it is not separately schedulable as its own epic.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-816ef491c81f9a1e","agent_id":"a10b6399675a8b73a","session_id":"b04d48ec-e92b-4b9b-98a0-90c74f405f25","uuid":"9c8371fb-e014-4114-b305-01a09e9ee013","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:06:02.951Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a493669515e74d19","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"cl