{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac7f1bb68ba025a8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E004\n3\ttitle: FIPS crypto remediation of serving data plane runtime images\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the audit finds the serving data plane images already link\n15\t    only validated crypto, this epic narrows to verification only; if source-level\n16\t    changes in upstream model-server projects are required, the approach is rewritten\n17\t    to include midstream patching or an upstream contribution.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: -1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 2\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# FIPS crypto remediation of serving data plane runtime images\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tMake every serving data plane model-server runtime image (vLLM, OpenVINO, Caikit-class runtimes) run correctly on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters using validated cryptographic modules, with no non-validated crypto in the inference request path. This epic also authors and verifies the FIPS regression gating check that covers serving runtime image builds.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Apply the remediation approach determined by the serving-stack crypto audit to each serving data plane runtime image identified as linking non-validated crypto (rebuild against validated modules, version changes, or library replacement, as documented in the audit's remediation plan).\n44\t- Verify the remediated runtime images on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster: model serving through the data plane exercises only validated crypto.\n45\t- Author and verify the FIPS regression gating check covering serving runtime image builds: the check fails any runtime build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage.\n46\t- Update the module inventory entries for the remediated runtime images to their post-remediation state, for consumption by the compliance evidence package.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t1. A post-remediation scan of every serving data plane runtime image in scope shows no non-validated cryptographic library in the request path.\n51\t2. The remediated images build green in the component build pipeline.\n52\t3. The remediated runtime images are verified to serve inference requests correctly on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster.\n53\t4. The FIPS regression gating check is active in the serving runtime build pipeline and demonstrably fails a build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage (verified against a known-bad case) while passing the remediated builds.\n54\t5. The module inventory entries for all remediated runtime images reflect the post-remediation state.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- HLR-1 (P0): serving data plane runtime images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules, with no non-validated crypto in the request path.\n59\t- HLR-3 (P1, bundled): the CI FIPS regression check covering serving runtime builds is authored and verified here — it spans the same build surfaces and remediated images as the HLR-1 work, so it is not separately schedulable as its own epic.\n60\t\n61\t## Risks / Notes\n62\t\n63\t- This surface is included because the problem statement names the serving data plane as linking non-validated crypto and HLR-1 requires all serving-stack images clean, even though the strategy's Affected Components list omits it; the discrepancy is recorded in the decomposition health warnings and should be confirmed with the strategy author.\n64\t- If source-level changes in upstream model-server projects prove necessary (rather than midstream rebuild-level changes), the remediation approach is rewritten to include midstream patching or upstream contribution.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f01b0db78708ef7","agent_id":"a16cf4daefa930ddb","session_id":"b04d48ec-e92b-4b9b-98a0-90c74f405f25","uuid":"fa223e75-0f28-476d-91e8-cbace0a6a94f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:15:36.629Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac7f1bb68ba025a8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9013"}
